  title="Caring for Your Silk"
  flagMessage="[DRAFT — general silk-care guidance. Review and adjust per piece before publishing.]"
>
  <p>Atlas ikat silk holds up well with a little care. General guidelines:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Hand wash in cold water with a gentle, pH-neutral detergent, or dry clean if you're unsure.</li>
    <li>Never wring — press gently between towels and lay flat to dry, out of direct sunlight.</li>
    <li>Iron on a low setting with a press cloth between the iron and the silk.</li>
    <li>Store away from direct light and humidity to keep the dye from fading or bleeding.</li>
    <li>Keep perfume and other sprays away from the fabric — they can mark silk permanently.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some pieces call for dry cleaning only — check the Care section on each product page for
    piece-specific instructions.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
